.TH CONFY 1 "2026-08-10" "3.1.0" "confy manual"

.SH NAME
confy \- a TUI config file manager for linux/unix systems

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B confy
.br
.B confy --web
.RI [ --gui | --text | --mode gui|text ]
.RI [ --ip address ]
.RI [ --port port ]
.RI [ --password password | --no-password ]
.RI [ -ni ]
.br
.B confy [action]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B confy
tracks your config files in one place so you don't have to remember where they all live.
add files to confy, organise them into groups, and open them in your
.B $EDITOR
with a single keypress. no more hunting through ~/.config.

written in rust using ratatui. zero required dependencies beyond the binary itself.

.SH NAVIGATION
.TP
.B j / k
or arrow keys \- move up and down the list
.TP
.B enter
open the selected file in
.BR $EDITOR ,
or toggle a group open/closed
.TP
.B space
toggle the selected group open/closed
.TP
.B p
toggle the live preview pane
.TP
.B /
enter search mode \- type to filter files and groups in real-time
.TP
.B :
enter command mode
.TP
.B q
quit

.SH COMMANDS
Commands are entered by pressing
.B :
followed by the command name and optional arguments, then
.BR enter .
.B esc
cancels.

.SS FILE MANAGEMENT
.TP
.B :ac
add a config file to the ungrouped group (opens the built-in file picker)
.TP
.B :ac <group>
add a config file directly to a named group
.TP
.B :rm
stop tracking the selected file (does not delete the file from disk)
.TP
.B :l
reopen the last edited file
.TP
.B :rb
rollback the selected file to its last backup (see
.BR ROLLBACK )
.TP
.B :diff
compare the selected file with each retained backup; press
.B r
to restore the selected version
.TP
.B :hooks
open
.I ~/.config/confy/hooks.toml
in the configured editor
.TP
.B :su
open the selected file as root via
.BR pkexec (1)
(requires polkit)
.TP
.B :import [chezmoi|stow|yadm]
review configs managed by a supported dotfile manager and choose which ones confy should track
.TP
.B confy import [chezmoi|stow|yadm]
open the same import review directly from the shell

.SS HOOKS
.B ~/.config/confy/hooks.toml
contains a
.B [hooks]
table with command arrays named
.BR opened ,
.BR changed ,
.BR rolled_back ,
.BR restored ,
.BR tracked ,
and
.BR untracked .
commands run asynchronously through
.BR sh (1)
and receive
.B CONFY_EVENT
and
.B CONFY_FILE
environment variables.

.SS COMMAND-LINE SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B confy l / confy last
open the last edited config before entering the tui
.TP
.B confy s:<text>
open the tui with search prefilled
.TP
.B confy o:<path> [g:<group>]
track and open a config file
.TP
.B confy d:<host>
switch to a remote device before opening the tui
.TP
.B confy stats / confy milestones
open the selected stats view directly
.TP
.B confy hooks
edit the hooks configuration
.TP
.B confy st:share
print copyable markdown stats and exit
.TP
.B confy st:img[:transparent], st:banner[:transparent], st:post[:transparent]
write a themed svg stats image in landscape, banner, or portrait format. the transparent form omits the canvas background
.TP
.B confy completions <bash|elvish|fish|powershell|zsh>
print a shell completion script
.TP
.B confy h / help / man
display usage information and exit
.TP
.B confy v / ver / version / e / edition
display version information and exit

.SS GROUP MANAGEMENT
.TP
.B :ag <group>
add a new group
.TP
.B :rg <group>
remove a group (files move to ungrouped)
.TP
.B :mg <group>
move the selected file to a group

.SS SORTING & SEARCH
.TP
.B :sort name
sort files alphabetically (default)
.TP
.B :sort date
sort by date last modified
.TP
.B :sort size
sort by file size
.TP
.B :reverse
toggle ascending/descending sort order

.SS APPEARANCE
.TP
.B :theme <name>
switch to a color theme. accepts any built-in theme or a custom theme
you've created. available built-in themes:
.BR catppuccin ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.BR nord ,
.BR tokyo-night ,
.BR one-dark .
applies instantly and persists across restarts.
.TP
.B :theme
list available built-in and custom themes
.TP
.B :theme list
list built-in and custom themes separately
.TP
.B :theme new
open the guided theme creator. walks you through naming the theme,
choosing a base theme or a blank template, then editing each color
component (background, foreground, highlight, group, border).
custom themes are saved as TOML files under
.IR ~/.config/confy/themes/ .
.TP
.B :theme delete <name>
delete a custom theme
.TP
.B :streamer
toggle streamer mode. hides full paths and timestamps, showing only filenames.
useful if you're recording your screen and don't want your username visible.

.SS CONFIGURATION DIRECTORY
.TP
.B :cd
change the config search directory used by the file picker (opens picker in dir-select mode)
.TP
.B :cd <path>
set the config search directory directly
.TP
.B :cd reset
reset the config search directory to
.I ~/.config

.SS REMOTE PROFILES
.TP
.B :device <host>
mount a remote machine's filesystem over sshfs and switch confy's view to that host's tracked configs.
accepts an
.I ~/.ssh/config
alias or a literal
.IR user@host .
requires
.BR sshfs (1)
installed locally.
.TP
.B :device local
unmount the remote and return to your local configs
.TP
.B :device
show the currently active device, if any
.TP
.B :ssh <host>
alias for
.B :device <host>

.SS GIT INTEGRATION
confy can manage a dotfiles git repository at
.I ~/dotfiles-git
(configurable). files are organised by group name; ungrouped files with a shared filename prefix are auto-foldered.
.TP
.B :git sync
copy all non-blacklisted tracked files into the dotfiles directory. no git operations performed.
.TP
.B :git commit
sync files, then prompt for a commit message and commit.
requires at least one prior commit to exist in the repo.
.TP
.B :git push
sync, commit (prompts for message), then push to the configured remote.
.TP
.B :git dir
change the dotfiles directory (opens picker)
.TP
.B :git dir <path>
set the dotfiles directory directly
.TP
.B :git reset
reset the dotfiles directory to
.I ~/dotfiles-git

.SS GIT BLACKLIST
.TP
.B :bl
toggle the selected file or group on/off the git blacklist.
blacklisted items are skipped by
.BR ":git sync" .
useful for .env files and other sensitive configs you don't want in a public repo.
.TP
.B :bouncer
open the bulk blacklist menu.
.B space
toggles an item,
.B Z
confirms,
.B esc
cancels.

.SS MISC
.TP
.B :h
.TQ
.B :help
show the first-startup tutorial again
.TP
.B :q
quit

.SH ROLLBACK
confy keeps the latest three gzip-compressed backups per tracked file under
.IR ~/.local/share/confy/backups/ .
it saves a backup before editing. if you break something, select the file and run
.B :rb
to restore it.

rollback can be disabled in
.IR config.toml :
.PP
.nf
[settings]
rollback = false
.fi

.SH WEB EDITOR
.B confy --web
interactively asks for a mode, ip address, port, and optional password before starting the browser editor. launch flags override their prompts; use
.B -ni
to skip the prompts and use defaults. the default mode is gui, on
.IR 127.0.0.1:3000 .
the gui provides the grouped file browser and command field; text mode provides an in-browser terminal with keybinds and a vim-style editor in jetbrains mono. both use the active theme. set
.B CONFY_WEB_PASSWORD
or pass
.B --password
to require basic authentication. use
.B --ip
and
.B --port
to choose another address. the built-in server uses http; use a tls reverse proxy when exposing it to a network. only tracked files are available.

.SH REMOTE PROFILES
.B :device <host>
mounts the remote machine's entire root filesystem over sshfs, then switches confy's view to that host's tracked configs. this means absolute paths like
.I /etc/pf.conf
resolve correctly through the mount.

if the remote is running an older version of confy (pre-config.toml, still on tracked.json), confy will refuse to connect and tell you to update confy on that host first.

.B :su
works through a mounted device: sshfs presents remote files under your own uid, so
.B pkexec
can elevate to local root and write through the mount even for root-owned remote files.

for
.B :su
to work through a device mount, your local machine needs
.I user_allow_other
uncommented in
.IR /etc/fuse.conf .
confy will tell you if this is missing.

.SH CONFIGURATION
confy stores its state in
.IR ~/.config/confy/config.toml .
if upgrading from an older version that used
.IR config.json ,
confy keeps the old file, copies it to
.I config.json.bak
and migrates the contents into
.I config.toml
on first run. an even older
.I tracked.json
is migrated automatically too.

.SS SETTINGS
all settings live under the
.I [settings]
table in config.toml:

.TP
.B rollback
boolean. save a backup before opening files for editing. default: true
.TP
.B theme
string. active color theme name. default: "catppuccin"
.TP
.B editor
string. override
.B $EDITOR
for opening files. useful for .desktop launchers where the env var may not be set.
.TP
.B streamer_mode
boolean. hide full paths and timestamps in the file list. default: false
.TP
.B streamer_hide_git
boolean. in streamer mode, also hide git-blacklisted files. default: true
.TP
.B ssh_allow
boolean. enable the
.B :device
sshfs integration. set to false if you don't use it. default: true
.TP
.B background_enable
boolean. draw a solid background color instead of the terminal default. default: false
.TP
.B background_color
string. hex color for the background when background_enable is true. default: "#1e1e2e"
.TP
.B colors
object. custom colors for the ui. supports hex codes (#rrggbb) and named colors
.RB ( black ,
.BR red ,
.BR green ,
.BR yellow ,
.BR blue ,
.BR magenta ,
.BR cyan ,
.BR white ,
.BR default ).
keys:
.BR bg ,
.BR fg ,
.BR highlight ,
.BR group ,
.BR border .

.SS GIT SETTINGS
.TP
.B git_dir
string. path to the dotfiles git repository. default: "~/dotfiles-git"
.TP
.B git_blacklist
array of strings. tracked file paths to exclude from
.BR ":git sync" .
.TP
.B git_blacklist_groups
array of strings. group names to exclude entirely from
.BR ":git sync" .
.TP
.B git_auto_push
boolean. reserved for future use. default: false
.TP
.B git_auto_commit
boolean. reserved for future use. default: false

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/confy/config.toml
main configuration and tracked file list
.TP
.I ~/.config/confy/config.json
legacy config from older versions. kept for reference after migration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/confy/config.json.bak
backup of the legacy config, created during migration
.TP
.I ~/.config/confy/themes/
custom theme definitions, one
.I <name>.toml
file per theme. each file uses the keys
.BR bg ,
.BR fg ,
.BR highlight ,
.BR group ,
and
.BR border .
.TP
.I ~/.cache/confy/mounts/
sshfs mountpoints for remote device profiles
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/confy/backups/
per-file rollback backups (gzip compressed, latest three retained)

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EDITOR
editor to open files with. overridden by the
.I editor
setting in config.toml. falls back to
.BR nano (1)
if neither is set.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# add a config file
:ac hyprland

# move it to a group
:mg hyprland

# search for a file
/hypr

# roll back after breaking something
:rb

# switch theme
:theme gruvbox

# browse a remote server's configs
:device myserver
:su
:device local

# set up dotfiles repo
:git dir ~/dotfiles
:git commit

# blacklist your .env before pushing
:bl
:git push
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sshfs (1),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR git (1)

